  "video_id": "SKsvU_hqTHs",
  "title": "This Free Tool Turns Any Project Into a Map You Can Actually Understand",
  "description": "Understand Anything is a free open source plugin with over 79,000 GitHub stars that turns any project into an interactive visual map. Every file and function becomes a box, with lines showing what connects to what. Click any box and it explains in plain English what that part does and why it exists, and it can walk you through your own project in the right order. Works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Copilot and Gemini CLI.\n\nGet the full install guide here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JtuA9bMX_2DePxfTXWkEydtYCNODoTTVsk3yoXRSG70/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #ClaudeCode #OpenSource",
